<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Utila</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Utila is the smallest of the three main <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-islands">Bay Islands</a> of Honduras, in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> near the southern end of the Mesoamerican Barrier Reef. English-speaking settlers from the Cayman Islands arrived in the 1830s, and it was part of the British Colony of the Bay Islands until its transfer to Honduras in 1860. It is now known for diving and whale sharks.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/utila.jpg" alt="Utila" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hoffryan at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Road_Near_Munchies,_Utila,_Honduras.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
